Spec: Feature Asynchronous Batch Regeocoding & WebP Export (2.4 / STAB-03 & STAB-05)

Purpose:
  Eliminate GUI-thread blocking and recursive call-stack growth in MainWindow::processNextRegeocodeLookup() and remove synchronous future.result() blocking in PictureWidget::exportSrcImgToWebpThread().

Platform: C++26 (Linux) / C++23 (Windows, macOS), Qt6

References:
  ../../../desktop-gallery.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /src/MainWindow.cpp
  /src/picture_widget.cpp
  /data/Prioritaetenliste.md

Must:
  Execute batch reverse geocoding in a background worker thread using an iterative loop rather than synchronous recursion on the GUI thread.
  Load the INI configuration, strategy priority list, and ReverseGeocoder instance once per batch instead of re-initializing them for every image.
  Isolate optional timezone lookup exceptions so address metadata is still written even if no timezone section is configured.
  Replace blocking future.result() in PictureWidget::exportSrcImgToWebpThread() with an asynchronous QMetaObject::invokeMethod callback on the GUI thread.

Must not:
  Call synchronous libcurl network requests or future.result() on the Qt GUI main thread.
  Use unbounded recursion to iterate through m_geoLookupQueue.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Refactor MainWindow::processNextRegeocodeLookup() in src/MainWindow.cpp to run iteratively in QtConcurrent::run with single-pass INI initialization.
  [x] #2 Replace future.result() blocking in PictureWidget::exportSrcImgToWebpThread() in src/picture_widget.cpp with an asynchronous GUI-thread callback.
  [x] #3 Verify compilation via cmake --build build and mark item 2.4 as completed in data/Prioritaetenliste.md.

Done when:
  cmake --build build succeeds without errors and both batch reverse geocoding and WebP export execute asynchronously without freezing the GUI thread.
